#!/bin/bash
# Kettle Linux, Pocket FIT Elite: after a wake-up, put back the rear buttons, which the MCU
# forgot while kernel 1446 had it powered off. Off the resume path: its driver needs about a
# second to bring the MCU back first.
[ "$1" = post ] || exit 0
[ -f /var/lib/kettle/rear-buttons ] || exit 0
systemd-run --no-block --collect --unit=kettle-rear-buttons-resume /usr/lib/kettle/kettle-rear-buttons restore >/dev/null 2>&1
exit 0
